{:edb/db-before-t 1536 :edb/db-after-t 1537 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534849 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:03:49.880Z" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186083207 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440931 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186105828 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440933 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186152275 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440930 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186177597 1078 #edb/ref 17592186177600 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186179988 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186179988 1071 "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=v-u,\\,y=u+v-1.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\n\nII. $det(A)=-2$\n\nIII. The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186179988 1071 "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$x = v - u, y = u + v - 1$.\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n2. $det(A) =-2$\n3. The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" 13194139534849 17592186045417 false] [17592186179988 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-u \\\\ u+v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+v \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 1=-2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186184160 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440932 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440905 1043 #edb/ref 17592186440934 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440905 1043 #edb/ref 17592186440935 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440905 1043 #edb/ref 17592186440936 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440905 1043 #edb/ref 17592186440937 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440905 1043 #edb/ref 17592186440938 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440905 1043 #edb/ref 17592186440939 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440905 1043 #edb/ref 17592186440940 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440905 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045460 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440905 1045 "Quiz 9" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440905 1046 #edb/ref 17592186440939 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440905 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440905 1053 #uuid "b54594b5-9269-55c1-947a-7f5c52c7cdb8" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440906 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440906 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440906 1083 #uuid "02156f42-01b9-5208-be76-46dd56d1f051" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [1759218