ref 17592186440908 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440927 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440911 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440927 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440918 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440927 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440924 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440927 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440927 1077 "selection" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440927 1078 #edb/ref 17592186440911 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440927 1079 #uuid "b50eac1f-2fd4-5e79-99ef-7e7a92a52cdc" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440928 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440906 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440928 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440912 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440928 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440913 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440928 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440921 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440928 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440925 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440928 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440928 1077 "selection" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440928 1078 #edb/ref 17592186440913 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440928 1079 #uuid "e2b3e7c5-52c2-5e4b-bcbf-08cf2d113f06" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440909 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440910 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440917 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440919 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186440923 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440929 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440929 1077 "selection" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440929 1078 #edb/ref 17592186440917 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440929 1079 #uuid "e453f27d-3265-5a94-8683-63394b11fa22" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440930 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440927 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440930 1069 "q-130992" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440930 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440930 1071 "For the differential equation $2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+xy={x}^{2}-x,$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440930 1072 #uuid "4ce39611-61f7-5873-a772-9d52755c9e24" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440930 1074 "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+xy=0.\n$$" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440931 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440929 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440931 1069 "q-122392" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440931 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440931 1071 "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{9}{16}{e}^{6x}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440931 1072 #uuid "c50fb833-030a-5f7e-b663-60682ede12d9" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440931 1074 "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{9}{16}{e}^{6x}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{9}{16}{e}^{6x}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\frac{3}{4}\\int {e}^{3x}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{4}{e}^{3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{3x}+4.$" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440932 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440928 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440932 1069 "q-130663" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440932 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440932 1071 "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]$, then ${A}^{4}=$" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440932 1072 #uuid "de50db69-1f49-5b62-bb8f-7cba652094a4" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440932 1074 "First, we compute ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${A}^{2}=A,$ so $A$ is an idempotent matrix. \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${A}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & ={A}^{2} \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{A}^{4}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440933 1068 #edb/ref 17592186440926 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440933 1069 "q-84194" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440933 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440933 1071 "A fair seven-sided die with sides labeled with numbers $1$ through $7$ is thrown once. If $X$ is the outcome of the die, what is the variance of $X?$" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440933 1072 #uuid "f4d37934-3250-5bec-8382-fecffdb8f8b8" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440933 1074 "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute the probability mass function $f(x).$ Here, there are $7$ possible outcomes ($1,2,3,4,5,6,7$) and each outcome has the same probability, so the probability mass function is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ |\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6)+7\\cdot f(7) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{7})+2(\\frac{1}{7})+3(\\frac{1}{7})+4(\\frac{1}{7})+5(\\frac{1}{7})+6(\\frac{1}{7})+7(\\frac{1}{7}) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4)+{5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6)+{7}^{2}\\cdot f(7) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{7})+4(\\frac{1}{7})+9(\\frac{1}{7})+16(\\frac{1}{7})+25(\\frac{1}{7})+36(\\frac{1}{7})+49(\\frac{1}{7}) \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =20-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =20-16 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440934 1058 #edb/ref 17592186440937 13194139534849 17592186045417 true] [17592186440934 1062 #uuid "2e680767-2f69-5742-9e88-d8